**Key result:** Brandt 2024 (TCC, IACR ePrint 2024/687) MKtP-diagonalisation does **not** extend to π(x) mod 2. Four orthogonal obstructions: (O1) hard string is oracle-dependent Kt-random prefix, not a fixed function; (O2) contradiction uses self-referential Kt on both sides; (O3) Chaitin-Ω density has no analog for fixed totals; (O4) produces uniform-time bounds, not circuit bounds — Brandt explicitly avoids the Williams/Hirahara algorithmic-method route precisely because that route faces T4. Verdict: FAIL/E.

