    721	| arXiv:2506.22634 TG-kernel "rigorous bound" for π(x) (Kılıçtaş-Alpay 2025) | FAIL | C+I | Paper claims ~1200 zeros suffice for π(x) at x with 10^8 digits via truncated-Gaussian Φ_TG(t)=e^{-t²} on [0,α] with cubic taper, plugged into Riesz-Weil explicit formula. Empirical falsification (S65, full PDF audited): (a) ∫Φ_TG(t)dt = 0.886 ≠ 0, so paper's premise F_TG(1)=0 (main term cancels) is self-contradictory — Φ_TG ≥ 0 on its support cannot integrate to 0; (b) S(x)=Σ Λ(n)Φ_TG(n/x) measured at x∈{100..30000} grows linearly as ≈0.886·x, NOT αe^{-α²}≈3.7×10⁻⁴ as paper derives — IBP on p.7 substitutes Ψ(t)≈t (PNT) and drops the (Ψ-t) deviation that encodes prime fluctuations, leaving an x-free identity; (c) Σ F_TG(ρ) is x-independent → cannot encode π(x) when "rounded"; (d) Lemma 2 zero-density bound N(σ,T)≤AT^{1-1/σ}(log T)^B at σ=1/2 gives AT^{-1}(log T)^B, decreasing in T, blatantly false (true (T/2π)log T grows); (e) Appendix B is symbolic-mysticism crank content ("EmbedS(Faruk Alpay):=Φ_∞... canonical identity fold"). The "smoothed-kernel beats explicit formula" idea is folklore: smoothing in log-scale with width h gives T·h ~ const, and integer-precision π(x) needs h ≲ log(x)/x ⇒ T ~ x. No polylog escape via this route. See experiments/wildcard/tg_kernel_audit.py | 65 |
    722	| Bernstein 2003 strengthened-gcd AKS variant (FOCUS-1 sub-attack 1) | FAIL | E (with weak C) | Tests whether the smaller-r AKS variant — augmenting the order condition `ord_r(n) > log²(n)` with a strong gcd test on the residual `(X+a)^n − (X^n + a) mod (n, X^r−1)` — admits a TC⁰-amenable formulation. Q1 on S47 22-sample n grid: empirical r already satisfies r/log²n mean = 1.207, mean (r − log²n) = 25.05, r prime in 21/22 cases. "Smaller r" is therefore empirical reality already; the question is *deterministic correctness* at this r. Q2/Q3 striking but expected: at canonical r, primes 3/3 pass, composites 0/13 pass, and Bernstein-style gcd of residual coefficients with n yields a non-trivial factor of n in **13/13 composite failures (incl. all 7 Carmichaels: 561, 1105, 1729, 2465, 2821, 6601, 8911)** — e.g. n=1729 → gcd(266, 1729) = 133 = 7·19 dividing 1729. Q4: dim/r ratio 0.9899 (identical to S47, no compression). Q5: even at r ≪ r_AKS (e.g. r = log₂(n)+1) the test discriminates the *specific* composites in our sample — the AKS bound is worst-case for adversarial near-primes, not typical composites. (E) The strengthened-gcd test still does length-O(log n) growing-dim r×r MPOW over Z_n (E5.3, unchanged) plus √φ(r)·log n integer-gcd checks of O(log n)-bit integers; integer gcd is in NC¹ (Hesse-Allender-Barrington 2002) but NOT known in TC⁰ — same NC¹/TC⁰ frontier as the MPOW it purportedly replaces. (Weak C) abandoning the order-condition bound to set r = log²(n) deterministically requires a sufficient certificate which is itself an AKS-style introspective-monoid argument. With FOCUS-1 sub-attacks 1 (this), 2 (S61, line 714), 3 (S64, line 719) all closed, **Chain E is computationally cornered**; only Brandt MKtP (FOCUS-3) and entirely-new lower-bound techniques remain. See experiments/circuit_complexity/aks_alternative/bernstein_smaller_r/. | 66 |
